.TH KIOSK-MODE 1 "August 2026" "gway-001" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kiosk-mode \- enable or disable the Arthexis HDMI kiosk with the bastion key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiosk-mode
[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBstatus\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiosk-mode
controls the host-local Arthexis HDMI kiosk manual override. The command uses
.B /usr/local/libexec/bastion-key-present
as the bastion USB verifier.
.PP
.B kiosk-mode on
creates a temporary manual kiosk state and starts
.B arthexis-hdmi-kiosk-layout.service
so the HDMI kiosk opens even while the verified key is present.
.PP
.B kiosk-mode off
removes that manual state and starts the layout service again. If the key is not
verified, disabling is refused and kiosk mode remains mandatory.
.PP
.B kiosk-mode status
prints the verifier state, manual state, kiosk service state, and state-file
path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/user/1000/arthexis-hdmi-kiosk/manual-enabled
Temporary manual kiosk state file.
.TP
.I /etc/default/arthexis-hdmi-kiosk
HDMI kiosk session environment.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1)
